# Full Support to Repel the Aggression

Condemning Pakistan's aggression on the Indian border and assuring that the DMK would offer its full support and cooperation in defeating the aggressor, Arignar Anna, General Secretary of the Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam, has issued a statement. The statement follows:

"On behalf of the Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam, I welcome the resolve expressed by the Prime Minister in his statement condemning Pakistan's blatant aggression.

"The Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam firmly declares that it will give the government its full support and cooperation.

"This critical moment must be treated as a call to unite the strength and support of every party and create solidarity in order to defeat the common problem of aggression. It is in a position to inspire and merit the appreciation of the people.

"The DMK wishes to point out that the Prime Minister should not remain satisfied merely with adhering to a ceasefire policy; he must demonstrate through action, in every way, his opposition to the aggressors.

"The DMK welcomes the Prime Minister's just insistence that 'we will not begin negotiations after allowing the aggressors to enjoy the fruits of aggression.'

"So far, the conduct of the great powers has proved futile. The DMK hopes that they will recognise their mistaken course and attempt to halt Pakistan's aggression.

"Although the Pakistani President's tours of Peking and Moscow have greatly diminished the diplomatic skill attributed to Pakistan's rulers, the support periodically given by the United States emboldens Ayub Khan to threaten that a full-scale war will erupt.

"Though we labour for world peace, this is the proper moment to show the world that we possess all the strength necessary to drive out aggressors.

"The DMK appeals to the Prime Minister to come forward, unite the members of every party, and transform them into a powerful force capable of performing the duty of protecting the nation's honour.

"At this moment, when a statesman of the highest order is urgently needed, the DMK firmly believes that Prime Minister Lal Bahadur will act in a manner worthy of that trust."

(*Samaneethi*, 14 September 1965)
